      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "<p>And with all this trouble within the academy, we were crushed and bent our heads to the ground in sorrow. We have no reshuyot [territories where the Jewish communities were considered to be under the jurisdiction of the geonim] from which to derive a livelihood [i.e., collect various taxes], for they were destroyed. Of those that remain, we were required to go [i.e., travel] to them ourselves, for the important scholars of the academy went out as judges in our jurisdiction. Also, our lands were destroyed and lost in those same harsh years that passed over us; our money and our lands were lost, and we were spilled out like the stones of the sanctuary at every street corner [see Lamentations 4:1]. We have bartered our treasures for food to keep ourselves alive [see Lamentations 1:11]. We have nothing left but the writings of our fathers. But God did not let our feet slip (Psalms 66:9), and our destroyer took pity on us and gave us our lives as booty, and with all that happened to us, we did not desert the ways of our fathers, and we studied His Torah</p>",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
